      "summary": "Causing death by doing an act with the intention of causing death, or with the intention of causing such bodily injury as is likely to cause death, or with knowledge that the act is likely to cause death.",
      "changes": "The foundational genus of all homicides is renumbered from Section 299 IPC to Section 100 BNS. The three mental states (Intention of death, Intention of likely fatal injury, Knowledge of likelihood) remain the conceptual bedrock of homicide law.",
