      "offense": "Information in Cognizable Cases (Mandatory Zero FIR, E-FIR & 14-Day PE)",
      "chapter": "Information to Police & Powers to Investigate",
      "badge": "Revolutionary Procedural Overhaul",
      "summary": "Every information relating to commission of cognizable offence given to an officer in charge of police station.",
      "changes": "Three monumental statutory transitions: (1) Zero FIR Statutory Right: Section 173(1) mandates that every police station MUST record information irrespective of the territorial jurisdiction where the crime was committed; (2) E-FIR: Allows electronic registration of complaints, provided the complainant physically signs within 3 days; (3) Preliminary Enquiry (S. 173(3)): In offences punishable between 3 to 7 years imprisonment, police may conduct a 14-day preliminary enquiry with prior permission of DSP before registering FIR to ascertain prima facie case.",
