      "offense": "Prosecution of Judges & Public Servants (120-Day Deemed Sanction)",
      "chapter": "Conditions Requisite for Initiation of Proceedings",
      "badge": "120-Day Deemed Sanction",
      "summary": "Prior sanction required before court takes cognizance of offences committed by public servants in discharge of official duty.",
      "changes": "Statutory deadline introduced: The sanctioning authority (Central/State Govt) MUST decide the sanction request within one hundred and twenty (120) days. If no decision is communicated within 120 days, sanction is DEEMED to have been accorded by operation of law under Section 218(1) proviso.",
      "cases": [
        "Subramanian Swamy v. Manmohan Singh (2012 4-month sanction rule)",
        "State of UP v. Paras Nath Singh (2009)"
      ],
      "duExamTip": "Section 218 BNSS eliminates endless administrative delays in corruption trials by enacting automatic deemed sanction at day 120."
