      "bnsNum": "57",
      "offense": "Primary Evidence (Cloud Storage & Simultaneous Digital Copies)",
      "chapter": "Documentary Evidence",
      "badge": "Cloud/Simultaneous Storage as Primary",
      "summary": "Primary evidence means the document itself produced for the inspection of the court.",
      "changes": "GROUNDBREAKING DIGITAL REFORM. Section 57 BSA Explanations 4 to 7 explicitly provide: (1) Where an electronic record is produced from proper custody, each copy created simultaneously in electronic form is PRIMARY EVIDENCE; (2) Where electronic files are stored across multiple cloud servers or system cache, each storage location is primary evidence.",
      "cases": [],
      "duExamTip": "Eliminates need for secondary evidence certificates when the primary electronic file or simultaneous cloud record is presented."
