      "offense": "Court May Presume Existence of Certain Facts (Natural Course & Stolen Goods)",
      "chapter": "Burden of Proof",
      "badge": "Discretionary Judicial Presumption",
      "summary": "Court may presume the existence of any fact which it thinks likely to have happened, regard being had to common course of natural events, human conduct, and business.",
      "changes": "Renumbered to Section 119 BSA. Retains iconic illustrations: (a) stolen goods recently after theft, (b) accomplice testimony uncorroborated, (c) bill of exchange, (g) evidence withheld would be unfavourable.",
